# Local build configuration, sourced by scripts/package-app.sh and
# scripts/install.sh when present. Copy this file to
# scripts/local.env (gitignored) and set CODESIGN_IDENTITY to a stable
# certificate so TCC grants and Keychain access survive rebuilds. A
# free self-signed code signing certificate created in Keychain Access
# also works. When unset, builds are ad-hoc signed and the code
# identity changes every rebuild.
#
# CODESIGN_IDENTITY="Developer ID Application: Name (TEAMID)"

# PROVISIONING_PROFILE: absolute path to a macOS Development
# provisioning profile (.provisionprofile). Required before
# scripts/Companion.entitlements can be applied: keychain-access-groups
# is an AMFI restricted entitlement, and an app that claims it without
# an embedded profile fails to launch (amfid -413, "No matching
# profile found"). When unset, signed builds skip the entitlement and
# stay launchable on the login keychain fallback.
#
# To mint one at developer.apple.com, Certificates Identifiers &
# Profiles:
#   1. Identifiers: register a wildcard macOS App ID (TEAMID.*). The
#      wildcard is required, not merely convenient: the keychain access
#      group follows each bundle's own identifier, so a build signs into
#      TEAMID.com.onetimesecret.companion,
#      TEAMID.com.onetimesecret.companion.backdrop, or the matching
#      .debug variant of either, and a profile has to authorize whichever
#      one it is. That is four ids, and one wildcard covers all of them.
#   2. Devices: register this Mac's Provisioning UDID (About This Mac,
#      System Report, Hardware, Provisioning UDID).
#   3. Profiles: create a "macOS App Development" profile against the
#      wildcard App ID, your development certificate, and this Mac.
#   4. Download it and point this variable at the file. It lives
#      happily anywhere; *.provisionprofile is gitignored.
#
# PROVISIONING_PROFILE="$HOME/Library/CompanionDev.provisionprofile"
